10	# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9011
11	
12	Adopt structured JSON logging across RHOAI components.
13	
14	## Triage
15	
16	Not below-threshold: the strategy spans 7 affected components owned by 6
17	distinct teams with HLRs at three priority levels — architecturally distinct
18	work streams warranting separate PR review cycles. Not documentation-only:
19	all affected components require code changes. Full decomposition follows.
20	
21	## Decomposition Approach
22	
23	The strategy is a textbook fan-out: one platform convention (HLR-1) is the
24	prerequisite design artifact, after which every per-component adoption is
25	independent ("Component adoptions are independent of each other once the
26	convention exists"). The strategy declares no open questions, no conditional
27	ADRs, no pending reviews, and no external dependencies — so no Investigation
28	epics and no tiered delivery. All components already exist in the platform
29	(architecture context files present for six; see Health Warnings regarding
30	Serving Runtimes), so no onboarding chains are generated.
31	
