9	# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9011
10	
11	Adopt structured JSON logging across RHOAI components.
12	
13	## Triage
14	
15	Not below-threshold: the strategy spans 7 affected components owned by 6
16	distinct teams with HLRs at three priority levels — architecturally distinct
17	work streams warranting separate PR review cycles. Not documentation-only:
18	all affected components require code changes. Full decomposition follows.
19	
20	## Decomposition Approach
21	
22	The strategy is a textbook fan-out: one platform convention (HLR-1) is the
23	prerequisite design artifact, after which every per-component adoption is
24	independent ("Component adoptions are independent of each other once the
25	convention exists"). The strategy declares no open questions, no conditional
26	ADRs, no pending reviews, and no external dependencies — so no Investigation
27	epics and no tiered delivery. All components already exist in the platform
28	(architecture context files present for six; see Health Warnings regarding
29	Serving Runtimes), so no onboarding chains are generated.
