29	# Publish platform structured logging convention
30	
31	## Description
32	
33	This epic delivers the platform-wide structured logging convention: the JSON
34	log schema, the set of required fields (timestamp, level, component,
35	namespace, correlation id), and library guidance per supported language (Go,
36	Python, TypeScript). It is the prerequisite design artifact that every
37	per-component logging adoption builds against; component adoptions cannot
38	start until it is published.
39	
40	## Scope
41	
42	- Define the JSON log schema: field names, types, and serialization rules for
43	  structured log records emitted by RHOAI components.
44	- Specify the required fields and their semantics: timestamp, level,
45	  component, namespace, and correlation id, including how a correlation id
46	  propagates across a user request that spans components (Dashboard, serving,
47	  pipelines).
48	- Write library guidance for each supported language (Go, Python,
49	  TypeScript): which logging library to use and how to produce
50	  convention-conformant records with the required fields populated.
51	- Publish the convention in a form that adopting teams can consume directly
52	  (schema plus per-language guidance).
53	
54	## Acceptance Criteria
55	
56	- A JSON schema for the structured log record exists and unambiguously
57	  defines the required fields: timestamp, level, component, namespace,
58	  correlation id.
59	- Library guidance exists for Go, Python, and TypeScript, sufficient for an
60	  adopting team to emit conformant records without further design work.
61	- The convention defines how a single user request is correlated across
62	  Dashboard, serving, and pipelines components.
63	- The convention is published and available to all adopting component teams.
64	- Given a raw log line from any adopting component, When it is parsed as
65	  JSON, Then all required fields are present and typed per the schema.
66	
67	## HLR Traceability
68	
69	- HLR-1 (P0): A platform logging convention is published: JSON schema,
70	  required fields, and library guidance per language.
