30	# Adopt convention-conformant logging in serving runtimes
31	
32	## Description
33	
34	The model serving runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit — the data-plane model
35	execution servers deployed by the serving stack) adopt the platform
36	structured logging convention so serving data-plane logs are
37	machine-queryable and correlatable with Dashboard and controller logs via
38	the correlation id.
39	
40	## Scope
41	
42	- For each serving runtime codebase, update logging to emit records
43	  conformant to the published platform JSON logging convention (following
44	  the convention's per-language guidance for each runtime's language).
45	- Populate the required fields on every log record: timestamp, level,
46	  component, namespace, correlation id.
47	- Ensure runtime log records identify their originating runtime in the
48	  component field so a query can distinguish runtimes.
49	
50	## Acceptance Criteria
51	
52	- Given a deployed serving runtime, When any log record is emitted, Then the
53	  record is valid JSON conforming to the platform convention schema with all
54	  required fields present (timestamp, level, component, namespace,
55	  correlation id).
56	- Given a model request processed by a serving runtime, When logs are
57	  queried by correlation id, Then the runtime's log records for that request
58	  are retrievable.
59	- No remaining ad-hoc (plain text / key=value) log output in runtime code
60	  paths covered by this adoption.
61	
62	## HLR Traceability
63	
64	- HLR-3 (P0, serving runtimes portion): Serving runtimes emit
65	  convention-conformant logs.
