30	# Adopt convention-conformant logging in Training Operator
31	
32	## Description
33	
34	The Training Operator (which runs distributed training jobs, primarily
35	PyTorchJob, admitted through Kueue) adopts the platform structured logging
36	convention so training job orchestration logs are machine-queryable and
37	correlatable via the correlation id.
38	
39	## Scope
40	
41	- Update Training Operator (Go) logging to emit records conformant to the
42	  published platform JSON logging convention per its Go library guidance.
43	- Populate the required fields on every log record: timestamp, level,
44	  component, namespace, correlation id.
45	
46	## Acceptance Criteria
47	
48	- Given the running Training Operator, When any log record is emitted, Then
49	  the record is valid JSON conforming to the platform convention schema with
50	  all required fields present (timestamp, level, component, namespace,
51	  correlation id).
52	- Given a distributed training job in a namespace, When logs are queried by
53	  namespace, Then the corresponding operator log records are retrievable.
54	- No remaining ad-hoc (plain text / key=value) log output in operator code
55	  paths covered by this adoption.
56	
57	## HLR Traceability
58	
59	- HLR-8 (P2): Training Operator emits convention-conformant logs.
